// Title: New BgInfo.EXE Custom VBScript Registry Configuration
// Sigma ID: 992dd79f-dde8-4bb0-9085-6350ba97cfb3
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects setting of a new registry value related to BgInfo configuration, which can be abused to
//   execute custom VBScript via "BgInfo.exe"
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate VBScript
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_bginfo_custom_vbscript.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Software\\Winternals\\BGInfo\\UserFields.*$" and RegistryValueData startswith "4"
